{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a detailed stitch task (#5081) from the cobbler orchestrator pipeline for the go-unix-utils project. The task is to implement core size string parsing logic in `pkg/sizeparse/parse.go`, replacing stub function bodies with working implementations that satisfy srd087-sizeparse requirements R1.1 through R1.4. The requirements cover: providing a Parse function (R1.1), supporting binary/IEC suffixes like K, KiB, M, MiB, b etc. (R1.2), supporting decimal/SI suffixes like KB, MB, GB etc. (R1.3), and preserving sign in the returned value (R1.4). The task includes strict constraints: no git commands, no filesystem exploration, no scope creep, imports limited to fmt/strconv/strings, function signatures must remain unchanged from the contract stubs.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Size string parsing with unit suffix multipliers (IEC binary powers of 1024 vs SI decimal powers of 1000)\n   - GNU coreutils suffix conventions (b=512, K=1024, KB=1000, KiB=1024, etc.)\n   - Go package contract design with exported types and functions\n   - int64 overflow handling for Z/Y suffixes whose multipliers exceed int64 range\n   - Delegation pattern: Parse delegates to ParseWithOptions with zero-value options\n   - Suffix table matching using a map with exact string matching after digit boundary split\n   - Sign handling gated by AllowSign option in ParseOptions\n   - DefaultUnit for bare numbers without suffixes (default 1, configurable e.g. 1024 for du)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd087-sizeparse.yaml`\n     - Read to understand full SRD requirements R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.2, R3.1-R3.2, non-goals, and acceptance criteria\n     - Key details: 26 suffix entries across IEC and SI, ParseOptions struct with AllowSign and DefaultUnit, Parse delegates to ParseWithOptions\n   \n   - `pkg/sizeparse/parse.go` (MODIFIED - this is the primary deliverable)\n     - Was stub with `return 0, nil` in both Parse and ParseWithOptions\n     - Replaced with full implementation\n     - Final implementation:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // Package sizeparse parses human-readable size strings (e.g. \"10K\", \"5M\") into\n     // byte counts. Implements srd087-sizeparse.\n     package sizeparse\n     \n     import (\n     \t\"fmt\"\n     \t\"strconv\"\n     )\n     \n     // ParseOptions configures size string parsing behavior.\n     type ParseOptions struct {\n     \tAllowSign   bool\n     \tDefaultUnit int64\n     }\n     \n     // R1.2: binary (IEC) suffix multipliers, R1.3: decimal (SI) suffix multipliers.\n     var suffixes = map[string]int64{\n     \t\"b\":   512,\n     \t\"K\":   1024,\n     \t\"KiB\": 1024,\n     \t\"KB\":  1000,\n     \t\"M\":   1 << 20,\n     \t\"MiB\": 1 << 20,\n     \t\"MB\":  1_000_000,\n     \t\"G\":   1 << 30,\n     \t\"GiB\": 1 << 30,\n     \t\"GB\":  1_000_000_000,\n     \t\"T\":   1 << 40,\n     \t\"TiB\": 1 << 40,\n     \t\"TB\":  1_000_000_000_000,\n     \t\"P\":   1 << 50,\n     \t\"PiB\": 1 << 50,\n     \t\"PB\":  1_000_000_000_000_000,\n     \t\"E\":   1 << 60,\n     \t\"EiB\": 1 << 60,\n     \t\"EB\":  1_000_000_000_000_000_000,\n     }\n     \n     // Z/Y suffixes exceed int64 range but must be recognized per R1.2/R1.3.\n     var overflowSuffixes = map[string]bool{\n     \t\"Z\": true, \"ZiB\": true, \"ZB\": true,\n     \t\"Y\": true, \"YiB\": true, \"YB\": true,\n     }\n     \n     // Parse parses a human-readable size string into a byte count.\n     // R1.1: delegates to ParseWithOptions with default options (no sign, unit=1).\n     func Parse(s string) (int64, error) {\n     \treturn ParseWithOptions(s, ParseOptions{})\n     }\n     \n     // ParseWithOptions parses a human-readable size string with configurable options.\n     // R1.1: accepts optional sign, decimal integer, and optional unit suffix.\n     func ParseWithOptions(s string, opts ParseOptions) (int64, error) {\n     \tif s == \"\" {\n     \t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid size: empty string\")\n     \t}\n     \tsign, numStr, suffix, err := splitParts(s, opts.AllowSign)\n     \tif err != nil {\n     \t\treturn 0, err\n     \t}\n     \tn, err := strconv.ParseInt(numStr, 10, 64)\n     \tif err != nil {\n     \t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid size %q: %w\", s, err)\n     \t}\n     \tmultiplier, err := resolveMultiplier(suffix, opts.DefaultUnit)\n     \tif err != nil {\n     \t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid size %q: %w\", s, err)\n     \t}\n     \t// R1.4: preserve sign in returned value.\n     \tresult := n * multiplier\n     \tif sign < 0 {\n     \t\tresult = -result\n     \t}\n     \treturn result, nil\n     }\n     \n     func splitParts(s string, allowSign bool) (int, string, string, error) {\n     \tsign := 1\n     \trest := s\n     \tif rest[0] == '+' || rest[0] == '-' {\n     \t\tif !allowSign {\n     \t\t\treturn 0, \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\n     \t\t\t\t\"invalid size %q: sign prefix not allowed\", s,\n     \t\t\t)\n     \t\t}\n     \t\tif rest[0] == '-' {\n     \t\t\tsign = -1\n     \t\t}\n     \t\trest = rest[1:]\n     \t}\n     \ti := 0\n     \tfor i < len(rest) && rest[i] >= '0' && rest[i] <= '9' {\n     \t\ti++\n     \t}\n     \tif i == 0 {\n     \t\treturn 0, \"\", \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"invalid size %q: no numeric value\", s)\n     \t}\n     \treturn sign, rest[:i], rest[i:], nil\n     }\n     \n     func resolveMultiplier(suffix string, defaultUnit int64) (int64, error) {\n     \tif suffix == \"\" {\n     \t\tif defaultUnit == 0 {\n     \t\t\treturn 1, nil\n     \t\t}\n     \t\treturn defaultUnit, nil\n     \t}\n     \tif overflowSuffixes[suffix] {\n     \t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"suffix %q exceeds int64 range\", suffix)\n     \t}\n     \tm, ok := suffixes[suffix]\n     \tif !ok {\n     \t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"unrecognized suffix %q\", suffix)\n     \t}\n     \treturn m, nil\n     }\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No runtime errors were encountered yet as verification commands (go build, go vet) have not been run.\n   - Design challenge: Z/Y suffixes (1024^7, 1024^8, 1000^7, 1000^8) have multipliers exceeding int64 range. Go would refuse to compile these as int64 constants. Solution: stored Z/Y suffixes in a separate `overflowSuffixes` map and return an immediate error when encountered, keeping them \"recognized\" (not \"unrecognized suffix\") but noting they exceed int64 range.\n   - Design tension: R1.1 describes \"optional sign\" in Parse's format but R2.1 says AllowSign defaults to false for Parse. Resolution: Parse with default options (AllowSign=false) rejects signs; sign handling is opt-in via ParseWithOptions with AllowSign=true.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved the suffix matching approach: since the suffix is extracted as the complete remaining string after digit boundary split, exact map lookup works without needing ordered longest-match-first iteration. The D2 design decision about longest-match-first is satisfied implicitly.\n   - Solved the int64 overflow problem for Z/Y multipliers by using a separate overflow detection map.\n   - Ensured all functions stay under 40 lines per E8 constitution requirement.\n   - Ensured exported signatures remain unchanged from the contract stubs (AC5).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The full stitch task prompt with embedded project context, SRDs, architecture, roadmap, execution constitution, go style constitution, task requirements, design decisions, acceptance criteria, constraints, and package contracts. This is the primary task assignment.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Instructions to provide a summary of the conversation without making any tool calls.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Run `go build ./pkg/sizeparse/...` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go vet ./pkg/sizeparse/...` to verify no issues (AC2)\n   - Verify AC3-AC5 are satisfied (Parse and ParseWithOptions are no longer stubs, all R1.1-R1.4 behaviors implemented, signatures unchanged)\n   - The task execution constitution says: \"Work is complete when all files are written and tests pass.\"\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was implementing task #5081 \"[stitch] srd087-sizeparse R1.1-R1.4: core size string parsing\". I completed writing the implementation file `pkg/sizeparse/parse.go` with the Write tool, replacing stubs with full parsing logic. The file was successfully written. I had not yet run the verification steps (go build, go vet) specified in the acceptance criteria before the summary was requested.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Run the acceptance criteria verification commands:\n   ```\n   go build ./pkg/sizeparse/...\n   go vet ./pkg/sizeparse/...\n   ```\n   This directly corresponds to the task's acceptance criteria AC1 and AC2, and the execution constitution article E5: \"Every item in Acceptance Criteria must be verified. Run tests if the criteria require it. Do not skip any criterion.\" The task description states: \"4. **Verify** — Check every item in Acceptance Criteria. Run tests if the criteria require it. Do not skip any criterion.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5081/f674801f-0862-4854-b494-5c4a46b54b47.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f674801f-0862-4854-b494-5c4a46b54b47","uuid":"dc82e96c-cd5d-4671-8277-7e7bd0346e2f","timestamp":"2026-05-13T22:47:27.382Z","isSynthetic":true}
